The content styles lay out the stack of blocks: each block is full width and flush at the top, and the gap after it is its own bottom padding, `--block-spacing-after`, so a block's background (the new `--block-background`) includes it, which defaults to the new `--block-spacing`. `--block-bottom-spacing` is renamed `--block-spacing-after`, and a block no longer passes it, nor its `--block-background`, on to the blocks nested in it: both are registered as non-inherited custom properties. `--justify-items` falls back to `stretch` instead of `start`. Removed rules that matched nothing: the `.block.narrow`, `.block.default` and `.block.layout` widths, `.content-area > .block`, the invalid `@property --block-width` and `main { grid-area }`. @danalvrz
